s of protein homology by assessing the (dis)similarity in protein loop regions</article-title><source>Proteins</source><year>2004</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>539</fpage><lpage>547</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15382231</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/prot.20237</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ponting</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of distant homologues of fibroblast growth factors suggests a common ancestor for all beta-trefoil proteins</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><year>2000</year><volume>302</volume><fpage>1041</fpage><lpage>1047</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11183773</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/jmbi.2000.4087</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Copley</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bork</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Homology among (betaalpha)(8) barrels: implications for the evolution of metabolic pathways</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><year>2000</year><volume>303</volume><fpage>627</fpage><lpage>641</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11054297</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/jmbi.2000.4152</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="other"><fpage>Supplementary data url for HCS paper.</fpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Structure/madej/hcs_tables.htm"/></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carpentier</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Brouillet</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Pothier</surname><given-names>J</given-names><